{"title":"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> represents a rectangular field. There are three flagpoles: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />. Paul runs along the path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/6/fe68ac3de642bf43bab0b8fc4fc96cb2bb6a293a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\to D \\to C \\to M \\to A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"192\" height=\"14\" />. Tyler runs along the path <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/2696f38503399e61f53d67422764517fa91edc78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A \\to P \\to Q \\to C \\to B \\to A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"228\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Paul and Tyler start running at the same time. Tyler runs at a speed of 145 m/min. Paul runs at a constant speed and finishes 1 minute after Tyler. Determine Paul’s speed, in m/min.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To determine Paul's speed, we must figure out both the distance of his path, as well as how long it takes for him to run across his path.\n</p><p>Opposite sides of rectangles are equal, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a783e0ff5c24fa009a66c9e3670018922a98516.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = BC = 200 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"155\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f2c74145e13dd1f37ec39d0c902a700fb4594e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = DC = 105 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"155\" height=\"14\" />. From the diagram, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/3/cc3b6d470b7ccc308e8a282a038a9cf6829b6343.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM + MB = BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/8/628e938f8be6c2bc530f455a102a8a8efa1359a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM + 100 = 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3d833803710ca8f7e80d78f5b224bb20d77ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM = 200 - 100 = 100 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"208\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a\" title=\"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a\">part a</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/a/18aef9452a34377005312877b44e5e0b990a6716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MA = 145 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"106\" height=\"14\" />. The total distance that Paul runs will just be the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/0/d9051721fef938a3ee8ac92dd6e9aba97a2d626d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ADCM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />, which would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/8/718947b917bd5e648d7b988a3ac6f22e1892c0c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD + DC + CM + MA = 200 + 105 + 100 + 145 = 550 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"466\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2b\" title=\"2018 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2b\">part b</a>, Tyler runs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/e/c7ef13d3d49f90ead0a6ba57913fdc7b583f6681.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$580 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> in total. This means that if he runs at a speed of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e3b11917cb488a1f68b5485729233c94db5549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$145 \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"61\" height=\"34\" />, he must take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c90bf8972311dc8581f58cee9faedb4e749dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{580}{145} = 4 \\text{ mins}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"106\" height=\"38\" /> in total. \n</p><p>Thus, if Paul takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/e/51e60e5610032e65a56fc7a84b2740a0718d424f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{ min}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> more minute, he must take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031e7e5e26a47dc04c822a7ee8daa96a0ed78266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ mins}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> in total.\n</p><p>Paul's speed would then be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/4/b04c934b6e9b9ff6b50a3030a2d9e102982165ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{550}{5} = \\boxed{110 \\frac{\\text{m}}{\\text{min}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"128\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018005314\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 85/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1213/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4332/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.265      1 2018_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n100.00%   14.265      1 -total\n 37.06%    5.286      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36939:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018005314 and revision id 285748. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}